      "headline": "Habit 7: Create Real Connections",
      "keyInsight": "Most people network like hungry seagulls chasing fries on a boardwalk. They dive down fast, snatch a business card, and flap away. But real influence behaves like rich garden soil. You cannot order a tomato plant to fruit in ten minutes. Plants need steady water, sunlight, and quiet care over time. When you treat people like vending machines, they immediately sense the hustle and close off. Counterintuitively, the quickest way to gain trust is to drop the quick pitch entirely. Take the clock off the wall. Listen to someone as if you have nowhere else to be. When you invest attention with zero agenda, human chemistry triggers a natural bond. Real persuasion is not a transaction. It is an enduring friendship built one honest chat at a time.",
